{
  "request": "Community grant application form for our town's small grants fund. Grants are for local groups running projects that bring people together. Include proper guidance notes, who can and can't apply, the organisation, the project, the difference it will make, a budget, safeguarding, bank details and a declaration signed by two people.",
  "title": "Community grant application",
  "description": "Use when a local group applies to the small grants fund: guidance and eligibility first, then the organisation, the project and its difference, the budget, safeguarding, bank details and a declaration signed by two people.",
  "maxPages": 8,
  "content": {
    "schemaVersion": 3,
    "branding": {
      "organizationName": "",
      "logoAsset": null,
      "logoDataUrl": null,
      "logoAlignment": "left",
      "logoWidthPercent": 24,
      "primaryColor": "#24543c",
      "accentColor": "#3f8f5e"
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Community grant application",
        "level": 1,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "This fund gives small grants to local groups for projects that bring people together and make the town a better place to live. Please read the guidance on these first pages before you start, and keep it beside you while you fill in the form.",
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Who can apply",
        "level": 2,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
        "type": "bullet_list",
        "items": [
          "Voluntary and community groups, registered charities, community interest companies and charitable incorporated organisations.",
          "Schools, health bodies and parish councils, for projects that go beyond what they must already provide.",
          "Your group must have a governing document, such as a constitution or set of rules, and a bank account in the group's name.",
          "At least two people who are not related, do not live at the same address and are not in a relationship must run the group and sign this form."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "What we cannot fund",
        "level": 2,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
        "type": "bullet_list",
        "items": [
          "Individuals, or projects that benefit only one person.",
          "Organisations that aim to make a profit for private gain.",
          "Activities that promote religious beliefs or a political party, although faith and political groups may apply for open community activities.",
          "Anything bought, or any activity that takes place, before we tell you our decision.",
          "Loans, fundraising events for other causes, or paying off debts."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "How much you can ask for",
        "level": 2,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The most and least you can ask for, how long a project can last and the closing date for each round are published with this form on the fund's web page. Ask only for what the project needs: a smaller, well-costed request is often stronger than a large one.",
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "How we decide",
        "level": 2,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "A panel of residents and council officers reads every eligible application. They ask four questions of each one:",
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
        "type": "numbered_list",
        "items": [
          "Need: is there a clear local need, and do you show how you know about it?",
          "People: have the people who will take part helped to plan the project?",
          "Difference: will the project bring people together, and will you be able to tell?",
          "Value: is the budget realistic, and does every cost relate to the project?"
        ],
        "itemRuns": [
          [
            {
              "text": "Need:",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is there a clear local need, and do you show how you know about it?"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "People:",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " have the people who will take part helped to plan the project?"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Difference:",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " will the project bring people together, and will you be able to tell?"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Value:",
              "bold": true
            },
            {
              "text": " is the budget realistic, and does every cost relate to the project?"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "How to fill in the form",
        "level": 2,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013",
        "type": "bullet_list",
        "items": [
          "Write in plain words, as if to someone who does not know your group. The panel only knows what you tell them.",
          "Answer every question. Where a question does not apply to you, say so.",
          "Attach your governing document and your most recent accounts, or bank statements for the last three months if your group is new.",
          "The main contact and the second contact must both sign the declaration in section 7."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "How we use your information: we use the details on this form to assess your application, to pay and monitor any grant, and to tell people about the projects we fund. We share them with the panel members who assess applications and with our auditors. We keep them for as long as our records retention schedule sets for grant files, which we will send you on request.",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "How we use your information:",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " we use the details on this form to assess your application, to pay and monitor any grant, and to tell people about the projects we fund. We share them with the panel members who assess applications and with our auditors. We keep them for as long as our records retention schedule sets for grant files, which we will send you on request."
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0a130000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Help: if you would like to talk about your idea before you apply, or need this form in another format, contact the grants team using the details on the fund's web page.",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "Help:",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " if you would like to talk about your idea before you apply, or need this form in another format, contact the grants team using the details on the fund's web page."
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
